## 1. What is the Salesforce Platform?

Salesforce is not just a CRM product — it is a **full cloud application platform**.
Businesses can use the built-in CRM apps out of the box, or build completely custom
applications on top of the same platform.

```
Salesforce Platform = Cloud infrastructure + CRM apps + App development environment
```

Think of it like Android: the OS (platform) already exists.
Developers build apps on top of it without touching the underlying infrastructure.

---

## 2. Multi-Tenant Architecture ⭐

**Multi-tenant** means many customers share the same Salesforce infrastructure
(servers, codebase, database engine), but each customer's data is completely
isolated and private.

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│             Salesforce Infrastructure             │
│  ┌───────────┐   ┌───────────┐   ┌─────────────┐ │
│  │ Company A  │   │ Company B  │   │    You      │ │
│  │  (data)   │   │  (data)   │   │   (data)    │ │
│  └───────────┘   └───────────┘   └─────────────┘ │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
         All on same platform — data is isolated
```

**Why it matters:**
- Salesforce handles all server maintenance, upgrades, and security
- Everyone automatically gets the latest version
- Scales with demand — no infrastructure work on your end
- Much cheaper than running dedicated servers

